    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1885-a3">

                <pb facs="1389" n="1273" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1273"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Consul General to Minister Price.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 24, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that I am instructed, by a cablegram recently received from my
                    Government, to express deep gratefulness to your excellency for the good offices
                    which your excellency used with an entirely satisfactory result in behalf of the
                    whole Chinese colony domiciled in the territory of the Republic of Panama, in
                    regard to the anti-Chinese legislation by the National Assembly of Panama, of
                    which I had informed my Government.</p>
                <p>In reference to the passports of those Chinese who might enter the United States,
                    I am instructed by our Minister in Washington that my Government had already
                    arranged with that of the United States that any Chinese who might <pb
                        facs="1390" n="1274" xml:id="pg1274"/> have the right to go into the
                    territory of the United States, and possessing a certificate issued by the
                    Chinese Consul General in Panama, should have the visé of the American Minister
                    or similar officials.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fong Tsiang Kwang.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
